ouching"}],"gloss":"touching the knees"},{"surface":"தடக்கை","parts":[{"text":"தட","lemma":"taṭa","gloss":"large"},{"text":"கை","lemma":"kai","gloss":"hand"}],"gloss":"large hands"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வழுவில்","parts":[{"text":"வழு","lemma":"vaḻu","gloss":"failure"},{"text":"இல்","lemma":"il","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without failure"},{"surface":"வன்கை","parts":[{"text":"வன்கை","lemma":"வன்கை","gloss":"strong hands"}],"gloss":"strong hands","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மழவர்","parts":[{"text":"மழவர்","lemma":"maḦavar","gloss":"warriors"}],"gloss":"of the Mazhavar warriors"},{"surface":"பெரும","parts":[{"text":"பெரும","lemma":"peruma","gloss":"lord"}],"gloss":"O Lord!"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இருநில","parts":[{"text":"இரு","lemma":"iru","gloss":"vast"},{"text":"நில","lemma":"nila","gloss":"earth"}],"gloss":"vast earth"},{"surface":"மண்","parts":[{"text":"மண்","lemma":"maṇ","gloss":"soil"}],"gloss":"land"},{"surface":"கொண்டு","parts":[{"text":"கொண்டு","lemma":"koṇṭu","gloss":"desiring"}],"gloss":"desiring"},{"surface":"சிலைக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"சிலைக்கும்","lemma":"cilaikkum","gloss":"roaring"}],"gloss":"roaring"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொருநரும்","parts":[{"text":"பொருநர்","lemma":"porunar","gloss":"fighters"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even fighters"},{"surface":"உளரோ","parts":[{"text":"உளர்","lemma":"uḷar","gloss":"exist"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"question"}],"gloss":"are there?"},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"nī","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"களம்","parts":[{"text":"களம்","lemma":"kaḷam","gloss":"battlefield"}],"gloss":"battlefield"},{"surface":"புகினே","parts":[{"text":"புகின்","lemma":"pukiṉ","gloss":"if enter"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"if you enter"}]}],"literal":"Like broken bangles blossomed flame lilies / with leaf-abundant wild jasmine fragrant mountain slopes / if fierce tiger rages, are there herds of deer? / In the directions of the darkened sky gathered / is there even darkness if the sun rages? / Striking with the axle, touching the ground and moving, / to resolve the sinking of the loaded cart, / crushing the spread sand and splitting stones, walks / the proud bull; is there any obstacle for it? / Resembling latch-bars, touching the knees, large arms, / unerring strong hands, O Lord of Mazhavar warriors! / Desiring the land of the vast earth and roaring, / are there even fighters if you enter the battlefield?","translation":"On the mountain slopes fragrant with wild jasmine rich in leaves, flame lilies blossom like broken bangles. If a fierce tiger rages there, can herds of deer stand against it? If the sun shines in fury, can any darkness remain in the directions of the darkened sky? To rescue a heavily loaded cart whose axle has struck the ground and sunk, a majestic bull walks, crushing the spread sand and splitting the stones under its hooves; is there any path or obstacle that can stop it? O Lord of the Mazhavar warriors, with long arms reaching to your knees like latch-bars and strong, unerring hands! If you enter the battlefield, are there any enemies left to roar, desiring the soil of this vast earth?","modern":"இலைகள் நிறைந்த காட்டு மல்லிகையோடு சேர்ந்து மணக்கும் மலைச்சாரலில், உடைந்த வளையல்களைப் போலக் காந்தள் மலர்கள் மலர்ந்துள்ளன. அங்கே சினங்கொண்ட புலி எதிர்த்தால் மான்கூட்டங்கள் தப்ப முடியுமா? கதிரவன் சினந்து எழுந்தால், இருண்ட வானத்தின் திசைகளில் திரண்டிருக்கும் இருள் எஞ்சியிருக்குமா? அச்சு முறிந்து தரையில் தட்டி நின்றுவிட்ட பார வண்டியின் துயரத்தைத் தீர்க்க, பரவிய மணல் நெரியவும் கற்கள் பிளக்கவும் கம்பீரமாக நடந்து செல்லும் பெருமிதம் கொண்ட எருதுக்குத் தடை என்று ஏதேனும் உண்டோ? கதவுக் தாழ்ப்பாள் போன்ற, முழங்கால் வரை தொங்கும் நீண்ட கைகளையும், தவறாத வலிமையான கரங்களையும் உடைய மழவர் தலைவனே! நீ போர்க்களத்தில் புகுந்தால், இந்த அகன்ற உலகத்தின் மண்ணைக் கைப்பற்ற எண்ணி ஆரவாரம் செய்யும் பகைவர்கள் எவரேனும் எஞ்சியிருப்பாரோ?","explanation":"This poem is addressed to the chieftain Athiyaman Neduman Anji by the famous poet Avvaiyar. It belongs to the tumpai tiṇai (warfare) and tāṉai maṟam tuṟai (the valor of the army/king). Avvaiyar praises Athiyaman's absolute supremacy in battle through three powerful analogies. First, she asks if a herd of deer can survive when a fierce tiger attacks. Second, she asks if darkness can persist when the sun shines in all its fury. Third, she compares him to a majestic, powerful bull that easily pulls a heavily loaded cart out of a rut, crushing sand and splitting stones, unstoppable by any obstacle. Through these vivid images of the mountain slopes, the tiger, the sun, and the mighty bull, the poet illustrates that no enemy can stand against Athiyaman once he enters the battlefield.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.1],[1.1,1.3],[1.3,1.5],[1.5,2.6],[2.6,2.8],[2.8,3.1],[3.1,3.7],[3.7,4.8],[4.8,5.1],[5.1,5.3],[5.3,5.9],[6.03,6.7],[6.7,7.2],[7.2,7.3],[7.3,7.7],[7.7,8.9],[8.9,9.1],[9.1,9.3],[9.3,9.9],[9.9,10.8],[10.8,11.47],[11.53,11.6],[11.6,12.1],[12.1,12.9],[12.9,13.0],[13.0,13.5],[13.5,13.7],[13.9,14.5],[14.77,15.1],[15.1,15.5],[15.5,15.9],[16.64,17.24],[17.24,17.74],[17.74,18.14],[18.14,18.24],[18.24,19.44],[19.44,19.74],[19.74,20.34],[20.34,20.74],[20.74,21.54],[21.54,21.74],[21.74,22.04],[22.04,22.64],[22.64,23.64],[23.64,23.84],[23.84,24.24],[24.24,24.64],[24.64,25.54],[25.54,25.64],[25.64,26.04],[26.04,26.14],[26.14,26.44]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,2.8],[2.8,3.7],[3.7,3.8],[3.8,4.4],[4.4,6.1],[6.1,6.3],[6.3,6.6],[6.6,7.2],[7.2,7.2],[7.2,9.0],[9.0,9.1],[9.1,9.6],[9.6,11.1],[11.1,11.3],[11.3,11.6],[11.6,12.2],[12.36,13.3],[13.3,13.67],[13.67,13.87],[14.0,14.7],[14.7,15.6],[15.6,15.8],[15.8,16.3],[16.3,16.6],[16.6,17.17],[17.4,18.23],[18.23,18.5],[18.5,19.0],[19.72,20.52],[20.52,21.12],[21.12,21.52],[21.52,21.72],[22.92,23.12],[23.12,23.42],[23.42,24.12],[24.12,24.52],[24.52,25.62],[25.62,25.92],[25.92,26.22],[26.22,26.92],[26.92,27.17],[27.17,27.17],[27.17,27.17],[27.17,29.42],[29.42,30.42],[30.42,30.52],[30.52,31.02],[31.02,31.12],[31.12,31.52]]},"sync":[[["உடைவளை","broken bangle"]],[["கடுப்ப","to resemble"]],[["மலர்ந்த","blossomed"]],[["காந்தள்","flame lily"]],[["அடைமல்கு","abundant with leaves"]],[["குளவியடு","with wild jasmine"]],[["கமழும்","fragrant"]],[["சாரல்","mountain slope"]],[["மறப்புலி","fierce tiger"]],[["உடலின்","if rages"]],[["மான்கணம்","herds of deer"]],[["உளவோ","are there?"]],[["மருளின","darkened"]],[["விசும்பின்","of the sky"]],[["மாதிரத்து","in the directions"]],[["ஈண்டிய","gathered"]],[["இருளும்","even darkness"]],[["உண்டோ","is there?"]],[["ஞாயிறு","sun"]],[["சினவின்","if rages"]],[["அச்சொடு","with the axle"]],[["தாக்கிப்","striking"]],[["பாருற்று","touching the ground"]],[["இயங்கிய","moved"]],[["பண்டச்","goods"]],[["சாகாட்டு","of the cart"]],[["ஆழ்ச்சி","sinking"]],[["சொல்லிய","to resolve"]],[["விரிமணல்","spread sand"]],[["ஞெமரக்","to crush"]],[["கல்பக","to split stones"]],[["நடக்கும்","walking"]],[["பெருமிதப்","proud"]],[["பகட்டுக்குத்","to the bull"]],[["துறையும்","even an obstacle"]],[["உண்டோ","is there?"]],[["எழுமரம்","latch-bar"]],[["கடுக்கும்","resembling"]],[["தாள்தோய்","touching the knees"]],[["தடக்கை","large hands"]],[["வழுவில்","without failure"]],[["வன்கை","strong hands"]],[["மழவர்","of the Mazhavar warriors"]],[["பெரும","O Lord!"]],[["இருநில","vast earth"]],[["மண்","land"]],[["கொண்டு","desiring"]],[["சிலைக்கும்","roaring"]],[["பொருநரும்","even fighters"]],[["உளரோ","are there?"]],[["நீ","you"]],[["களம்","battlefield"]],[["புகினே","if you enter"]]]}